course: dictionary
lesson: 4407
title: Halite: rock salt
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Halite is the scientific name for rock salt, the same kind of salt you put on your chips. Scientists call it a mineral, which is a natural solid with a set chemical makeup. «Rock salt (halite) is a mineral that formed when ancient seas dried up.» The sentence tells you two things: halite is a mineral, and it is salt left behind when water dried away.
explain: Notice the brackets in the sentence. They give the scientific name in the middle of a plain phrase, so you can link «rock salt» with the word halite. When you meet a new science word, look for brackets, commas or a dash that explain it. Then check: does your meaning fit the sentence?
explain: Context also tells you how halite forms. The sentence says it formed when ancient seas dried up. As water dries, the salt it carried is left behind, and over a very long time that salt builds up into solid rock. Ancient means very old, so this happened a very long time ago.
fact: Halite means rock salt, the natural mineral form of table salt.
fact: Halite is made of sodium chloride, the same chemical as table salt.
fact: Halite often forms clear or white crystals shaped like cubes.
fact: Halite forms when salty seas or lakes dry up.
fact: People mine halite for salt for food and to grit icy roads.
exercise: «Rock salt (halite) is a mineral that formed when ancient seas dried up.» What is halite another name for? | Coal | Sugar | *Rock salt | Chalk
exercise: Which word in «Rock salt (halite) is a mineral that formed when ancient seas dried up» means very old? | seas | dried | formed | *ancient
exercise: Halite crystals are often shaped like what? | Needles | Spirals | Balls | *Cubes
test: Why do people mine halite? | To make paper | To make blue paint | *For salt for food and to grit icy roads | To build houses from bricks
test: In «Rock salt (halite) is a mineral», what do the brackets show? | *The scientific name for rock salt | A list of colours | A joke | A date
exam: Halite crystals are cubes. Which 3D shape from maths is a cube? | *Cube | Pyramid | Sphere | Cone
